          "id": "india-cpi-october-6pct-2026-11-12",
          "lead": true,
          "importance": 5,
          "verified": true,
          "headline": "Retail inflation hits 6.09% in October, above the RBI's 6% upper limit",
          "summary": "Consumer prices rose 6.09% from a year earlier in October, up from 5.54% in September, MoSPI data showed on Thursday. It is the first breach of the RBI's 2-6% tolerance band in two years and the highest reading in the new 2024-base series. Food inflation jumped to 8.94% from 7.74%, led by onions (up 116%), garlic and ginger; rural inflation was 6.63% and urban 5.41%.",
          "why_it_matters": "ICRA's chief economist says a 25 bp repo rate hike at the Dec 2-4 RBI meeting now looks almost certain, which would raise loan costs.",
          "published_at": "2026-11-12T16:12:38+05:30",
          "tags": [
            "Inflation",
            "CPI",
            "RBI",
            "Food prices"
          ],
